 </i></span> tend to be published in lower impact factor journals (<span style=\"color: rgba(105, 219, 99, 1.0); font-weight: bold;\">8<sup>th</sup></span> percentile among all words)  and tend to be cited less (<span style=\"color: rgba(255, 168, 82, 1.0); font-weight: bold;\">0<sup>th</sup></span> percentile word). In general, this word is positively associated with university ranking, such that higher-ranked institutions are more likely to publish papers containing <span style=\"color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 1.0); \"><i>\"hta\" </i></span> (<span style=\"color: rgba(170, 117, 250, 1.0); font-weight: bold;\">99<sup>th</sup></span> percentile). "}